          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Robert Fulton's Early Life</strong><br>\nRobert Fulton was born in Pennsylvania in 1765 to Irish immigrants. He initially worked as a painter, but his interest in mechanics led him to engineering and inventing, shaping transportation history.</p>\n\n<p><strong>From Art to Engineering</strong><br>\nFulton's shift from art to engineering occurred when he moved to England. There, he gained patrons who supported his interest in canal navigation, leading to his designs for aqueducts, canal systems, and submarines.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Submarine \"Nautilus\"</strong><br>\nDuring his time in France, Fulton built the \"Nautilus,\" one of the earliest submarines, in 1800. It was used for experimental dives and pitched for naval warfare, demonstrating the potential of underwater navigation.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
